---
const skills = [
  { name: 'Go', icon: 'go' },
  { name: 'PostgreSQL', icon: 'postgresql' },
  { name: 'Java', icon: 'java' },
  { name: 'Python', icon: 'python' },
  { name: 'Unity', icon: 'unity' },
  { name: 'Docker', icon: 'docker' },
];
---
<div id="skills" class="skills">
  <p>Here are a few of the technologies I use to build projects:</p>
  <ul class="technology-badges">
    {skills.map(skill => <li><img src={`/icons/${skill.icon}.svg`} alt="" width="32" height="32" loading="lazy" /><span>{skill.name}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <details class="more-skills"><summary>More technologies</summary><p>SQL, C#, HTML/CSS, Bash, SQLite, SQLAlchemy, Git, GitHub Actions, Oracle Cloud, Unix/Linux, REST APIs, Webhooks, and Postman.</p></details>
</div>
